    definition: '''Vehicle and plant exhaust contains combustion products such as nitrogen oxides, carbon monoxide, particulate matter and hydrocarbons. Emissions depend on engine condition, fuel, load, maintenance, idling and operating pattern. Exhaust can accumulate in poorly ventilated areas and contribute to ambient air pollution.''',
    purpose: '''The objective is to reduce unnecessary combustion emissions, prevent localized exposure, improve equipment efficiency and meet applicable fleet, permit and workplace requirements. Priority is source reduction and maintenance rather than relying only on distance or PPE.''',
    regulatoryBasis: '''Check current UAE vehicle/equipment rules, project specifications, authority permit conditions and occupational requirements for enclosed or semi-enclosed work. Applicable requirements vary by equipment class, location and activity; verify before asserting a numerical emission limit.''',
    procedure: '''Select fit-for-purpose equipment; maintain engines and exhaust systems; prohibit unnecessary idling through site rules; plan routes and loading to reduce trips; avoid running combustion equipment in enclosed spaces without a suitable engineered ventilation and exposure assessment; investigate visible abnormal exhaust; record defects and remove unsafe plant from service.''',
    documents: '''Plant register; inspection and preventive maintenance records; idling-control procedure; fuel-use records where tracked; equipment certificates; enclosed-area ventilation assessment; defect and corrective-action reports.''',
    documentOwnership: '''Plant manager owns fleet condition; operators perform pre-use checks; maintenance provider repairs defects; HSE and Environmental teams assess exposure and environmental impact; project leadership enforces idling and procurement rules.''',
    verification: '''Check service status, exhaust leaks, smoke/odour complaints, operating locations and idle time; verify ventilation and atmospheric monitoring where occupational exposure risk exists; retain repair evidence.''',
    commonErrors: '''Using visible smoke alone as the only emissions indicator; allowing diesel engines to idle near occupied areas; operating combustion plant in confined or poorly ventilated spaces; ignoring exhaust leaks.''',
    fieldExample: '''A generator positioned near a site office is relocated or exhaust is safely directed after assessment, maintained to manufacturer requirements, and monitored for complaints and exposure risks.''',
